  "cil_liability": true,
  "subdivision_of_building": null,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun within 3 years from the date of this permission.\r\nReason: To prevent the accumulation of unimplemented planning permissions and to comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended) and to meet the requirements of Section 51 of the Planning and Compulsory Purchase Act 2004 and to meet the requirements of The Town and Country Planning (Development Management Procedure) (England) Order 2015.\r\n",
    "Condition : 2 - The development shall be carried out in accordance with: \r\nDrawings number: EX_1; EX_2; EX_3; EX_10; EX_11; EX_12; EX_50; P_3 rev a; P10; P_11; P_12; P_50; EX_20; EX_21; EX_22; EX_23; EX_51; P_20; P_21; P_22; P_23; P_51.\r\nDocuments: \r\n- Cover Letter; prepared by: Savills; dated: 28/04/2026; titled:  APPLICATION UNDER SCHEDULE 2, PART 3, CLASS MA -RIVER HOUSE & PARK HOUSE, POINT PLEASANT, SW18 1NN; \r\n- Transport Statement: titled: CAERUS DEVELOPMENTS LTD- CHANGE OF USE-PARK HOUSE AND RIVER HOUSE,POINT PLEASANT, WANDSWORTH; prepared by: Mayer Brown; project code: CDPointPleasant.1; dated: 15/04/2026. \r\n- Flood Risk Assessment: Site Address: Park House and River House; prepared by: aegaea; reference: AEG8441_SW18_Wandsworth_01A; dated: 13/04/2026. \r\n- Noise Impact Assessment: titled: Point Pleasant London SW18; prepared by: quantum acoustics; reference: QA25317/NIA/Rev2; dated: 13/04/2026.\r\n- CONTAMINATED LAND DESK STUDY AND PRELIMINARY RISK ASSESSMENT: titled: PARK AND RIVER HOUSE, POINT PLEASANT, WANDSWORTH SW18; dated: 31/03/2026; prepared by: Wilson Bailey; reference: J26017/c01a/DB\r\n- Daylight and Sunlight Report: titled: River House and Park House, Point Pleasant; prepared by: Eb7; reference 7198; dated 14/04/2026. \r\n\r\nReason: To ensure a satisfactory standard of development and to allow the Local Planning Authorityto review any potential changes to the scheme.\r\n",
    "Condition : 3 - Any building permitted to be used as a dwellinghouse by virtue of Class MA is to remain in use as a dwellinghouse within the meaning of Class C3 of Schedule 1 to the Use Classes Order and for no other purpose, except to the extent that the other purpose is ancillary to the use as a dwellinghouse.\r\n\r\nReason: In accordance with the provision of Class MA of Schedule 2, Part 3 of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended). \r\n\r\n",
    "Condition : 4 - Prior to first occupation, details of a scheme of sound insulation measures designed to protect the development from externally generated noise sources, including road traffic, rail, and aircraft noise, have been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The scheme shall demonstrate that internal ambient noise levels within the development will not exceed the guideline values set out in Table 4 of BS 8233:2014, Guidance on Sound Insulation and Noise Reduction for Buildings. \r\nMeasured or calculated noise levels shall be determined in accordance with BS 8233:2014. \r\nAny works forming part of the approved scheme shall be completed in accordance with the approved details prior to first occupation of the dwellings and shall thereafter be retained as approved.\r\n\r\nReason: To protect the amenities of neighbouring occupiers, in accordance with policies LP1 and LP2 and LP14 of the Local Plan.\r\n\r\n",
    "Condition : 5 - Prior to the installation of any fixed plant or equipment associated with the development, a noise control scheme shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The scheme shall demonstrate compliance with the following noise design criterion and the approved measures shall thereafter be retained and maintained for the lifetime of the development.\r\nThe cumulative measured or calculated rating level of noise emitted from all fixed building services plant and equipment shall be at least 5 dB(A) below the existing background sound level at all times when the plant is operating.\r\nThe rating level and background sound level shall be determined in accordance with the methodology set out in the current version of BS 4142. Assessment shall be undertaken at the boundary of the nearest ground-floor noise-sensitive premises, or at a position 1 metre from the fa�ade of the nearest first-floor (or higher) noise-sensitive premises. \r\n\r\nAlternative assessment locations may be agreed where necessary to facilitate access, if these are clearly identified on a site plan and supported by appropriate acoustic calculations demonstrating compliance with the required criterion.\r\n\r\nReason: To protect the amenities of neighbouring occupiers, in accordance with policies LP1 and LP2 and LP14 of the Local Plan.\r\n",
    "Condition : 6 - A) If, during development, contamination not previously identified is found to be present at the site then no further development (unless otherwise agreed in writing with the local planning authority) shall be carried out until the developer has submitted, and obtained written approval from the local planning authority for, a remediation strategy detailing how this unsuspected contamination shall be dealt with. The remediation strategy shall be implemented as approved, verified and reported to the satisfaction of the Local Planning Authority. \r\n\r\nB) Prior to first occupation:  If a remediation strategy is submitted to and approved by the local planning authority in relation to part 1 of this condition, the remediation shall be completed in accordance with that strategy then a verification report produced, and then submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\r\n\r\nReason: To ensure that risks from land contamination to the future users of the land and neighbouring land are minimised, together with those to controlled waters, property and ecological systems, and to ensure that the development can be carried out safely without unacceptable risks to workers, neighbours and other off-site receptors, having regard to Council policy LP14 of the Local Plan coupled with the requirements of the National Planning Policy Framework.\r\n\r\n\r\n",
    "Condition : 7 - Prior to the first occupation of the development, the relevant building's cycle parking as shown on the approved drawing shall be provided, and be retained for cycle parking purposes for the users of the development and for no other purpose.\r\n\r\nReason: To ensure adequate provision is made for cycle parking in accordance with Council policies LP2, LP37, LP51, PM2, PM3, PM4, PM6, PM7, PM8 and PM9 of the Wandsworth Local Plan coupled with the requirements of the National Planning Policy Framework.\r\n",
    "Condition : 8 - Prior to occupation a Car Park Management Plan (CPMP) shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The CPMP shall include, but not limited to, the following: \r\ni) Provision of three disabled parking bays to be made available from first occupation of the development;\r\nii) Details of a mechanism for the provision of additional disabled parking spaces to serve up to 7% of the total number of dwellings of this application, where demand for accessible parking exceeds the initial provision, including trigger points, delivery timescales and arrangements for monitoring demand;\r\niii) Parking bays ownership scheme; \r\niv) Management of car parking across the site, \r\nv) Details of the provision of electric vehicle charging infrastructure, including the installation of charging facilities for 20% of all parking spaces associated with this application from the outset, together with passive provision for the remaining parking spaces associated with this application to enable the future installation of electric vehicle charging facilities;\r\n\r\nReason: To encourage sustainable transport and ensure accessibility, in accordance with Council policies LP2, LP37, LP51, PM2, PM3, PM4, PM6, PM7, PM8 and PM9 of the Wandsworth Local Plan, policies T2, T5, T6, and T6.1 of the London Plan (2021) coupled with the requirements of the National Planning Policy Framework.\r\n",
    "Condition : 9 - Prior to the first occupation of the development, the relevant building's refuse and recycling storage shown on approved drawings shall be provided and shall be retained for the users of the development and for no other purpose.\r\n\r\nReason: To ensure adequate provision is made for waste storage in accordance with Council policies LP1 and LP2 of the Wandsworth Local Plan coupled with the requirements of the National Planning Policy Framework.\r\n"
  ],
